n (42 [67%] of 63 patients), and erythrocyte sedimentation rate (30 [52%] of 58 patients), but not procalcitonin.", pmid:"32176772", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32176772"}}, {start: {_id:386}, end: {_id:568}, properties:{evidence:"In terms of inflammation indicators, patients on admission showed increase in lactate dehydrogenase (25 [41%] of 61 patients), c reactive protein (42 [67%] of 63 patients), and erythrocyte sedimentation rate (30 [52%] of 58 patients), but not procalcitonin.", pmid:"32176772", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32176772"}}] AS row
