 included anaemia and increased alanine transaminase (ALT)", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:885}, end: {_id:857}, properties:{evidence:"Interesting, smog and nicotins also favour lung inflammation increasing ACE activity and, therefore, affecting ACE2 functionality.", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:886}, end: {_id:857}, properties:{evidence:"Interesting, smog and nicotins also favour lung inflammation increasing ACE activity and, therefore, affecting ACE2 functionality.", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:887}, end: {_id:73}, properties:{evidence:"ACE inhibitors, AT1R blockers and mineralocorticoid receptor blockers (MRB), pioglitazone and ibuprofen included, are reported to have direct effects on suppression of the ACE-Ang II-AT1R axis, often increasing ACE2 and Ang (1–7) significantly, in contrast with the inhibitory effects on the ACE2-ANG(1-7) axis by glucocorticoids", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:888}, end: {_id:73}, properties:{evidence:"ACE inhibitors, AT1R blockers and mineralocorticoid receptor blockers (MRB), pioglitazone and ibuprofen included, are reported to have direct effects on suppression of the ACE-Ang II-AT1R axis, often increasing ACE2 and Ang (1–7) significantly, in contrast with the inhibitory effects on the ACE2-ANG(1-7) axis by glucocorticoids", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:889}, end: {_id:73}, properties:{evidence:"ACE inhibitors, AT1R blockers and mineralocorticoid receptor blockers (MRB), pioglitazone and ibuprofen included, are reported to have direct effects on suppression of the ACE-Ang II-AT1R axis, often increasing ACE2 and Ang (1–7) significantly, in contrast with the inhibitory effects on the ACE2-ANG(1-7) axis by glucocorticoids", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_i