ionType:"biorxiv", citationRef:"https://doi.org/10.1101/2020.03.22.002386"}}, {start: {_id:1360}, end: {_id:1256}, properties:{annotationExperiment:["Literature derived"], evidence:"Chemoinformatics searches yielded 15 approved drugs, four investigational new drugs (clinical), and 18 pre-clinical candidates (Table 1a), while specialist knowledge revealed 12 approved drugs, 10 investigational new drugs (clinical), and 10 preclinical candidates (Table 1b).", citationType:"biorxiv", citationRef:"https://doi.org/10.1101/2020.03.22.002386"}}, {start: {_id:1467}, end: {_id:1442}, properties:{evidence:"The used TLR3 agonists, poly ICLC and poly (I:C) (polyinosinic:polycytidylic acid) could augment the production of IFN-α, -β, and -γ, which consequently inhibited CoV replication and compensated for the inhibitory effects of CoV on IFN signaling pathways.", annotationCell:["naive T cell"], citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0206.v2"}}, {start: {_id:1467}, end: {_id:944}, properties:{evidence:"The used TLR3 agonists, poly ICLC and poly (I:C) (polyinosinic:polycytidylic acid) could augment the production of IFN-α, -β, and -γ, which consequently inhibited CoV replication and compensated for the inhibitory effects of CoV on IFN signaling pathways.", annotationCell:["naive T cell"], citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0206.v2"}}, {start: {_id:1467}, end: {_id:440}, properties:{evidence:"The used TLR3 agonists, poly ICLC and poly (I:C) (polyinosinic:polycytidylic acid) could augment the production of IFN-α, -β, and -γ, which consequently inhibited CoV replication and compensated for the inhibitory effects of CoV on IFN signaling pathways.", annotationCell:["naive T cell"], citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0206.v2"}}, {start: {_id:1471}, end: {_id:922}, properties:{evidence:"In addition to TLR-3 agonists (poly ICLC, poly (I:C), and rintatolimod) and phytohaemagglutinin (PHA) can induce IFN production in the human body as well.", annotationCell:["naive T cell"], citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0206.v2"}}] AS row
