ecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:221}, properties:{evidence:"The SARS-CoV (beta coronavirus), 229E (alpha 65coronavirus), HKU1 (beta coronavirus), NL63 (alpha coronavirus), OC43 (beta coronavirus) and MERS-CoV (beta coronavirus) can cause infectiousness in humans", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:311}, properties:{evidence:"Later on, during June 2012 a patient infected by MERS-CoV developed severe pneumonia and died in Jeddah, Saudi Arabia", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:515}, properties:{evidence:"Later on, during June 2012 a patient infected by MERS-CoV developed severe pneumonia and died in Jeddah, Saudi Arabia", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:320}, end: {_id:515}, properties:{evidence:"According to situation report 35, published on the WHO website, SARS-CoV-2 caused 79331 confirmed cases and 2618 deaths around the globe", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:234}, end: {_id:516}, properties:{evidence:"Both MERS and SARS patients in later stages develop respiratory distress and renal failure", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:516}, properties:{evidence:"Both MERS and SARS patients in later stages develop respiratory distress and renal failure", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:333}, end: {_id:588}, properties:{evidence:"Commonly documented adverse effects of ribavirin included anaemia and increased alanine transaminase (ALT)", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:586}, end: {_id:593}, properties:{evidence:" Corticosteroids use on the current outbreak was widely reported. However, the current evidence indicates that the benefit of general use is inconclusive and is likely outweighed by adverse effect (delayed viral clearance, avascular necrosis, osteoporosis, diabetes, psychosis)", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:586}, end: {_id:594}, properties:{evidence:" Corticosteroids use on the current outbreak was widely reported. However, the current evidence indicates that the benefit of general use is inconclusive and is likely outweighed by adverse effect (delayed viral clearance, avascular necrosis, osteoporosis, diabetes, psychosis)", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:586}, end: {_id:410}, properties:{evidence:" Corticosteroids use on the current outbreak was widely reported. However, the current evidence indicates that the benefit of general use is inconclusive and is likely outweighed by adverse effect (delayed viral clearance, avascular necrosis, osteoporosis, diabetes, psychosis)", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:586}, end: {_id:595}, properties:{evidence:" Corticosteroids use on the current outbreak was widely reported. However, the current evidence indicates that the benefit of general use is inconclusive and is likely outweighed by adverse effect (delayed viral clearance, avascular necrosis, osteoporosis, diabetes, psychosis)", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:424}, end: {_id:690}, properties:{evidence:"Although the long use of this drug in malaria therapy demonstrates the safety of acute chloroquine administration to humans, one cannot ignore the minor risk of macular retinopathy, which depends on the cumulative dose [52], and the existence of some reports on cardiomyopathy as a severe adverse effect caused by