:302}, end: {_id:217}, properties:{evidence:"The SARS-CoV (beta coronavirus), 229E (alpha 65coronavirus), HKU1 (beta coronavirus), NL63 (alpha coronavirus), OC43 (beta coronavirus) and MERS-CoV (beta coronavirus) can cause infectiousness in humans", pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:232}, end: {_id:216}, properties:{evidence:"The SARS-CoV (beta coronavirus), 229E (alpha 65coronavirus), HKU1 (beta coronavirus), NL63 (alpha coronavirus), OC43 (beta coronavirus) and MERS-CoV (beta coronavirus) can cause infectiousness in humans", pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:296}, end: {_id:217}, properties:{evidence:"The SARS-CoV (beta coronavirus), 229E (alpha 65coronavirus), HKU1 (beta coronavirus), NL63 (alpha coronavirus), OC43 (beta coronavirus) and MERS-CoV (beta coronavirus) can cause infectiousness in humans", pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:217}, properties:{evidence:"The SARS-CoV (beta coronavirus), 229E (alpha 65coronavirus), HKU1 (beta coronavirus), NL63 (alpha coronavirus), OC43 (beta coronavirus) and MERS-CoV (beta coronavirus) can cause infectiousness in humans", pmid:"32161092", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32161092"}}, {start: {_id:551}, end: {_id:314}, properties:{evidence:"Lopinavir/ritonavir, protease inhibitors for human immuno deficiency viruses (HIV) management, were reported to reduce mortality, intubation rate, and use of methylpred-nisolone when introduced as a treatment among SARS patients of early stage.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:585}, end: {_id:314}, properties:{evidence:"Lopinavir/ritonavir, protease inhibitors for human immuno deficiency viruses (HIV) management, were reported to reduce mortality, intubation rate, and use of methylpred-nisolone when introduced as a treatment among SARS patients of early stage.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:224}, end: {_id:537}, properties:{evidence:"Remdesivir, an antiviral agent, has been shown effectively inhibiting the COVID-19 in vitro and in vivo, , is under clinical trials, and compassionate use was reported on a deteriorating case with good recovery.", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:786}, end: {_id:539}, properties:{evidence:"Teicoplanin, a glycopeptide antibiotic routinely used to treat bacterial infection was found to be active in vitro against SARS-CoV, has joined the list of molecules that could be used as herapeutic arsenal against COVID-19 [7]", pmid:"32179150", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32179150"}}, {start: {_id:844}, end: {_id:849}, properties:{evidence:"Angiotensin II (ANGII) is a peptide hormone that can bind the type 1 angiotensin II receptor (AT1), giving place to a number of effects that result in vasoconstriction and, therefore, in increased blood pressure.", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:250}, end: {_id:931}, properties:{evidence:"Indeed, based on our findings and the proposed framework, it is reasonable to hypothesize that some inhibitors of autophagy (e.g., chloroquine, currently undergoing clinical trial, cf. Table 1) would prevent the virus from entering the host cell and could thereby be used to prevent SARS-CoV-2 infections while activators of autophagy (e.g., interferon-alpha 2a/2b, also undergoing clinical trial), which would help the host cell clear the viral particles, could be used to treat severe forms of COVID-19.", annotationDisease:["Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2"], citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}, {start: {_id:560}, end: {_id:957}, properties:{evidence:"Rapamycin activator of autophagy immunosuppressant; anticancer agent", citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}, {start: {_id:560}, end: {_id:958}, properties:{evidence:"Rapamycin activator of autophagy immunosuppressant; anticancer agent", citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}, {start: {_id:959}, end: {_id:958}, properties:{evidence:"Temsirolimus activator of autophagy anticancer agent", citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}, {start: {_id:960}, end: {_id:957}, properties:{evidence:"Tacrolimus activator of autophagy immunosuppressant", citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}] AS row
