: {_id:585}, end: {_id:227}, properties:{evidence:"Lopinavir/ritonavir, protease inhibitors for human immuno deficiency viruses (HIV) management, were reported to reduce mortality, intubation rate, and use of methylpred-nisolone when introduced as a treatment among SARS patients of early stage.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:551}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"Lopinavir/ritonavir, protease inhibitors for human immuno deficiency viruses (HIV) management, were reported to reduce mortality, intubation rate, and use of methylpred-nisolone when introduced as a treatment among SARS patients of early stage.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:585}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"Lopinavir/ritonavir, protease inhibitors for human immuno deficiency viruses (HIV) management, were reported to reduce mortality, intubation rate, and use of methylpred-nisolone when introduced as a treatment among SARS patients of early stage.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:333}, end: {_id:227}, properties:{evidence:"Ribavirin was also widely used in SARS based on the broad spectrum antiviral activity.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:333}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"Ribavirin was also widely used in SARS based on the broad spectrum antiviral activity.", annotationSpecies:["9606"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:592}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:" Interferons have also been shown to suppress the viral replication of SARS in vitro and been considered for the current outbreak ", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:224}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"Remdesivir, an antiviral agent, has been shown effectively inhibiting the COVID-19 in vitro and in vivo, , is under clinical trials, and compassionate use was reported on a deteriorating case with good recovery.", annotationBioassay:["in vivo", "in vitro"], pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:616}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"The treatment  under  evaluation  included  (1)  public  health  intervention:  community-based prevention programme, (2) pharmacological therapy: corticosteroid (glucocorticoid,methylprednisolone), antivirals  (darunavir,  cobicista,  lopinavir/ritonavir,  azvudine,arbidol, remdesivir, favipiravir, triazavirin, interferon), antimalarials (chloroquine/hydroxychloroquine), antibiotics (carrimycin), immunomodulators (tocilizumab,fingolimod,leflunomide), anti-allergic drug (Tranilast), sodium aescinate and CMs, (3) biologics:mesenchymal stem cell, immunoglobulin/convalescent plasma, microbiota transplantation,PD-1 blocking antibody, recombinant cytokine gene-deprived protein and bevacizumab,(4) supplements: alpha lipoic acid, vitamin C and probiotics, and (5) other therapies: M1 macrophage suppression therapy, hydrogen–oxygen nebulizer, ultra-short wave electro-therapy, and nutrition support.", pmid:"32164424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32164424"}}, {start: {_id:617}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"The treatment  under  evaluation  included  (1)  public  health  intervention:  community-based prevention programme, (2) pharmacological therapy: corticosteroid (glucocorticoid,methylprednisolone), antivirals  (darunavir,  cobicista,  lopinavir/ritonavir,  azvudine,arbidol, remdesivir, favipiravir, triazavirin, interferon), antimalarials (chloroquine/hydroxychloroquine), antibiotics (carrimycin), immunomodulators (tocilizumab,fingolimod,leflunomide), anti-allergic drug (Tranilast), sodium aescinate and CMs, (3) biologics:mesenchymal stem cell, immunoglobulin/convalescent plasma, microbiota transplantat