ntary Table 1 and Table 2. Antifungal agent did not show influence on the outcome of COVID-19 patients. And use of corticosteroids were associated with a higher risk of death.", pmid:"32176772", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32176772"}}, {start: {_id:424}, end: {_id:407}, properties:{evidence:"Recently, chloroquine was found to inhibit SARS-CoV-2 in vitro and its hydroxylated form has been proposed as a possible therapy to treat patients infected with SARS-CoV-2 [4,5].", pmid:"32179150", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32179150"}}, {start: {_id:786}, end: {_id:407}, properties:{evidence:"Teicoplanin, a glycopeptide antibiotic routinely used to treat bacterial infection was found to be active in vitro against SARS-CoV, has joined the list of molecules that could be used as herapeutic arsenal against COVID-19 [7]", pmid:"32179150", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"32179150"}}, {start: {_id:842}, end: {_id:838}, properties:{evidence:"As an example, recently, a number of specific anti-cytokine approaches have proven effective in treating a variety of cytokine storm syndromes, including those triggered by coronaviruses.", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:842}, end: {_id:386}, properties:{evidence:"As an example, recently, a number of specific anti-cytokine approaches have proven effective in treating a variety of cytokine storm syndromes, including those triggered by coronaviruses.", citationType:"arXiv", citationRef:"arXiv:2003.11614v1"}}, {start: {_id:932}, end: {_id:933}, properties:{evidence:"For instance, statins, anti-diabetics, and antagonists of the angiotensin receptor 1, which are used to treat hyperlipidemia, type 2 diabetes, and hypertension, respectively, all of which are very common diseases. ", citationType:"preprints", citationRef:"10.20944/preprints202003.0302.v1"}}] AS row
MATCH (start:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row.start._id})
